2026-05-21 18:58:05 -0700
fix(deploy): hardcode --branch=main; wrangler-action doesn't expand env vars in command

The previous `--branch=$DEPLOY_BRANCH` shipped the literal string
`$DEPLOY_BRANCH` because cloudflare/wrangler-action@v3 passes the
`command:` value to its own runner which does NOT expand shell env
vars. Result: CF Pages used its fallback alias
`deploy-branch.port-daddy.pages.dev` instead of promoting the
deploy to the production alias `portdaddy.dev`. The site stayed
on the previous (empty-body) deployment.

Hardcode `--branch=main` (matching the project's production_branch
on Cloudflare Pages) so the deploy lands at the prod alias
directly. The workflow_dispatch input is unused now and dropped.


